      "#vendor-table \"Overall score is the equal-weight mean of all required category scores. Vendors missing a publishable category are not ranked. Intervals describe uncertainty in the preserved judged sample; unresolved differences are not evidence of equivalence. \"Won outright\" counts queries where one vendor alone took the highest ensemble median; \"among best\" counts queries where it was level with the highest. Those differ a great deal here, because {latest.wins.n_tied} of {latest.wins.n_queries_compared} queries ended in a tie, which is itself the most useful thing this table says.\" [Vendor | Score & evidence | Cost / query | Run cost | p50 latency | Won outright | Among best | Scored | Returns]",
